Mostly because those are "special" trophies.

We started the first Tournament with just the per-class tropies, since those
were the obvious way to map NetHack onto the traditional structure of a
sporting event (i.e. Olympic gold, silver and bronze).

The two ascension trophies were suggested by players as good measures of
NetHack skill.  We've always thought of the Tournament as having two styles of
trophy, the "standard" per-class trophies (only one of which can go to any
particular player) and the "special" trophies.

It's been suggested that we add runners up to the scoreboard just as an
informational feature, which I'm more inclined to do than to add second and
third spots to the special trophies.

-robin

